Portuguese editions and parallel readings (@greek-portuguese-editions: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-sources, #contains @greek-source-nova-cultural, #contains @greek-source-plato-pt, #contains @greek-source-epictetus-pt) { r_3DABDPGKRDSM682Q2NYDEVX4Z8
These editions can supply the reading text for the same question as an English edition. Use the work, author, translator, and passage to identify a reading; keep the terms and numbering of each edition visible when comparing them.

| Edition | Use | Access |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Os pré-socráticos, Nova Cultural](Presocratics-Nova-Cultural.lingua#r_6ZA1ENV6PB59E6EGC7MCBS1782) | Fragments, ancient testimony, and commentary across [the earlier Greek readings](../presocratics/Nature-and-being.lingua#r_61M87EN28QQ9AHXT80SPCB0CVH) | Library or the reader's own copy |
| [Apologia de Sócrates / Críton, EdUFPA](Apology-Crito-Nunes.lingua#r_5653D0KAK9093C4VMSTEZJ3MBW) | The [Apology](../socratic/Apology.lingua#r_0DWAPFJNVYT6WNTRT46ZVK82X4) and [Crito](../socratic/Crito.lingua#r_54N10WGKCSCKW6XM202PCG7ZDH) questions, with parallel Greek | Publisher, library, or the reader's own copy |
| [O Encheirídion de Epicteto, Dinucci and Julien](Epictetus-Dinucci-Julien.lingua#r_0T9SP89H4SNVSN6XV25QY7EF9W) | [Judgment, agency, and duties](../schools/Epictetus.lingua#r_35EWPVCFYNWZ0DYG5R5HM05TC2) | Open Portuguese translation in the UFS repository |

**Comparison exercise:** choose one short exchange or fragment. Reconstruct its argument in Portuguese or English, compare a key term in another translation, and explain whether the difference affects the reasoning. Translation is evidence to examine; the preferred language does not determine a correct interpretation.

